# Ocentra Games – Security Testing Guidelines (MANDATORY)

> This document defines **mandatory security testing, coverage tooling, and setup** for this repository.
>
> The system is a **money-critical, Solana-based blockchain game backend** with a decoupled architecture (Cloudflare is NOT a trusted boundary).
>
> This spec is authoritative. Cursor MUST set up tooling and tests accordingly.

---

## Document Purpose & Scope

This document defines **HOW to test security** (tooling, CI mechanics, test setup).

**This document does NOT define:**

- Security guarantees and threats (see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc`)
- Test quality standards (see `ocentra-test-rules.mdc` §0.2)
- How to write tests (see `ocentra-test-rules.mdc`)

**Key Principle:**
> For security guarantees and numbered rules, refer to `ocentra-security-rules.mdc`.  
> For test writing standards, refer to `ocentra-test-rules.mdc`.

---

## 0. NON-NEGOTIABLE SECURITY PRINCIPLES

These principles align with security guarantees defined in `ocentra-security-rules.mdc`:

- **Coding with AI is guaranteed to screw up without tests** - See §2.9 for comprehensive testing checklist
- Line coverage ≠ security coverage
- Cloudflare ≠ security boundary
- Client input is hostile
- Concurrency is a first-class threat
- Partial failure must be economically neutral (see Rule 0.1.1 in `ocentra-security-rules.mdc`)
- Replay must never produce profit (see Rule 0.1.1 in `ocentra-security-rules.mdc`)
- Security failures must fail CI
- Time is a first-class adversary (see Rule 0.1.2 in `ocentra-security-rules.mdc`)
- Internal APIs are as hostile as public ones (see Rule 0.1.5 in `ocentra-security-rules.mdc`)
- Backend must never sign what it cannot independently verify (see Rule 0.1.3 in `ocentra-security-rules.mdc`)
- Attacker cost ≥ system cost (see Rule 0.1.1 in `ocentra-security-rules.mdc`)
- Compensation paths must be idempotent and replay-safe (see Rule 0.1.1 in `ocentra-security-rules.mdc`)
- Emergency controls must reduce blast radius, not increase it (see Rule 0.1.5 in `ocentra-security-rules.mdc`)
- Tests themselves are security-critical

