### 2.9 COMPREHENSIVE TESTING TOOLING REFERENCE (AI CODING CHECKLIST)

> **CRITICAL:** When coding with AI, tests are **guaranteed to be missing or incorrect** unless explicitly verified. This section provides a comprehensive reference of testing categories and tools that MUST be considered for every code change.

**AI MUST reference this section when:**
- Writing new code
- Refactoring existing code
- Adding features
- Fixing bugs
- Reviewing pull requests

**Rule:**
> Coding with AI without tests = guaranteed bugs. Every code change MUST include appropriate tests from the categories below.

#### 2.9.1 Foundation Testing (Unit | Integration | E2E)

**Required for all code changes:**

- **Unit Tests**: Vitest | Jest | JUnit
  - Test individual functions/modules in isolation
  - Fast execution, high coverage
  - Must test edge cases, not just happy paths

- **Integration Tests**: Vitest | Jest | Testcontainers
  - Test component interactions
  - Real database (Testcontainers), not mocks
  - Seeded prod-like data

- **E2E Tests**: Cypress | Playwright
  - Full user workflows
  - Browser automation
  - Real user interactions

**AI Checklist:**
- [ ] Unit tests cover all branches
- [ ] Integration tests use real dependencies (no mocks for money logic)
- [ ] E2E tests cover critical user flows
- [ ] Tests fail when code is broken (verify by temporarily breaking code)

---

#### 2.9.2 Advanced Testing Techniques (Invariant | Property-Based | Mutation | Differential)

**Required for logic and economic code:**

- **Invariant Testing**: fast-check | Hypothesis
  - Properties that must ALWAYS be true
  - Economic invariants (balance ≥ 0, no double-spend)
  - State invariants (valid transitions only)

- **Property-Based Testing**: fast-check | Hypothesis
  - Generate random inputs, verify properties hold
  - Find edge cases automatically
  - Log counterexamples on failure

- **Mutation Testing**: Stryker
  - Verify tests detect bugs
  - Only on `@mutation`-decorated code (see `ocentra-mutation-rules.mdc`)
  - Mutation score ≥ 80% for decorated code

- **Differential Testing**: diff-test harness
  - Compare implementations
  - Verify consistent behavior
  - Catch regression bugs

**AI Checklist:**
- [ ] Property-based tests for all economic logic
- [ ] Invariants explicitly stated and tested
- [ ] Mutation testing enabled for critical logic (with `@mutation` decorator)
- [ ] Counterexamples logged for property test failures

