## 4. COVERAGE REQUIREMENTS (FAIL CI IF VIOLATED)

CI MUST FAIL IF:

- Any money-critical endpoint lacks required test categories (see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 14.16):
  - negative tests
  - replay tests
  - concurrency tests
  - rollback/compensation tests
  - economic exhaustion tests
  - time-based attack tests
  - signing/verification tests
- Any invariant test fails (see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 0.1.1-0.1.6)
- Schemathesis finds new failing cases
- Coverage thresholds drop
- Kill-switch tests are missing (see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 15.7)
- Test integrity violations (non-deterministic tests, shared state) - see `ocentra-test-rules.mdc` §11
- Property-based tests fail without logging counterexamples
- Fuzz tests fail without logging seeds

---

## 5. REQUIRED CI PIPELINE STEPS

1. Install dependencies
2. Run unit + coverage tests
3. Run property-based tests (with counterexample logging)
4. Run API fuzzing (with seed persistence)
5. Run concurrency tests (limited)
6. Run Solana localnet tests (including signing abuse tests - see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 3.1, 3.2)
7. Run static analysis
8. Verify observability hooks (see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 15.8)
9. Run rollback/compensation tests (see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 12.1.1, 12.1.2)
10. Run economic exhaustion tests (see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 15.4)
11. Run time-based attack tests (see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 15.3)
12. Run test integrity checks (order independence, no shared state) - see `ocentra-test-rules.mdc` §11
13. Verify threat model → test mapping completeness (see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 15.9)

---

## 6. DOCUMENTATION & TRACEABILITY

Every money-critical endpoint MUST document:

- Economic invariants (see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 0.1.1)
- Idempotency scope
- Replay behavior
- Failure behavior
- Rollback/compensation behavior (see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 0.1.4)
- Time-based assumptions (cooldowns, expiry) - see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 0.1.2
- Signing/verification requirements (see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 0.1.3)
- Economic cost analysis (attacker cost vs system cost) - see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 0.1.1
- Threat model mapping (which threats this endpoint addresses) - see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 15.9

Every test MUST document:

- Which threat(s) it addresses (reference specific rules from `ocentra-security-rules.mdc`)
- Which invariant(s) it verifies (reference Rule 0.1.1-0.1.6 from `ocentra-security-rules.mdc`)
- Reproducibility requirements (seeds, inputs)
- Failure conditions (what breaks if this test fails)

---

## 7. FINAL RULE

If a test only verifies a happy path, it is NOT a security test.

This spec overrides convenience.

### 7.1 Security Test Quality Checklist

A security test is valid only if (see also `ocentra-test-rules.mdc` §20 and `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 13):

- [ ] It fails when protection is removed
- [ ] It asserts exact rejection behavior
- [ ] It does NOT rely on "no crash"
- [ ] It tests behavior, not configuration
- [ ] It assumes a hostile client
- [ ] It maps to an explicit threat in the threat model (reference `ocentra-security-rules.mdc`)
- [ ] It verifies an invariant (reference `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 0.1.1-0.1.6)
- [ ] It is reproducible (deterministic seeds/logs)

If any box is unchecked → **test rejected**.

### 7.2 Common Security Test Failures

**BANNED PATTERNS:**

- Tests that pass when logic is deleted
- Tests that only assert "success"
- Tests without explicit threat mapping (must reference `ocentra-security-rules.mdc`)
- Non-reproducible fuzz tests
- Tests with shared mutable state
- Tests that depend on execution order
- Property-based tests without counterexample logging

**REQUIRED PATTERNS:**

- Explicit threat → test mapping (reference `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` sections 1-15)
- Invariant verification (reference `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 0.1.1-0.1.6)
- Economic cost analysis (see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 0.1.1)
- Time-based assumption testing (see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 0.1.2)
- Rollback/compensation idempotency (see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 0.1.4)
- Signing/verification correctness (see `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` Rule 0.1.3)

